<article class="env-lemma" id="0BRG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BRG">Lemma <span data-tag="0BRG">15.112.6</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $G$ be a finite group of order $n$ acting on $R$. Let $A$ be an $R^ G$-algebra. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for $b \in (A \otimes _{R^ G} R)^ G$ there exists a monic polynomial $P \in A[T]$ whose image in $(A \otimes _{R^ G} R)^ G[T]$ is $(T - b)^ n$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for $a \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(A \to (A \otimes _{R^ G} R)^ G)$ we have $(T - a)^ n = T^ n$ in $A[T]$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a surjection $E \to A$ where $E$ is a polynomial algebra over $R^ G$. Then $(E \otimes _{R^ G} R)^ G = E$ because $E$ is free as an $R^ G$-module. Denote $J = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(E \to A)$. Since tensor product is right exact we see that $A \otimes _{R^ G} R$ is the quotient of $E \otimes _{R^ G} R$ by the ideal generated by $J$. In this way we see that our lemma is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/0H35" data-tag="0H35">15.112.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>